## Preserve exactly

- Layout and visual hierarchy (hero, KPIs, analytics, Quick Actions, bookings, payments, upcoming events, album metrics, footer)
- Crystal/glass surfaces, borders, shadows, glows, cinematic lighting, particles, and animations
- Colors, gradients, accent treatments, and icon sizes/styles
- Typography and spacing
- Responsive breakpoints
- Existing Dashboard functionality, API calls, calculations, permissions, routes, and data behavior

## Other work must stay independent

Work on other modules without touching the files above.

If you must change shared CSS or layout shells:

- Do not alter `.dhara-dashboard`, `.dhara-dash-*`, `.dhara-erp-shell`, `.dhara-erp-sidebar`, `.dhara-erp-header`, or `dashboard-page.css` / `erp-chrome.css`.
- Scope new styles so they cannot override Dashboard or ERP chrome descendants.
- Prefer new class names over changing globals used by the Dashboard or sidebar/header.

Do not restyle the sidebar or header “for the whole app” unless the user explicitly asked for a Dashboard/chrome change.

## Allowed exception

Only modify the Dashboard (or the locked chrome files listed above) when the user clearly asks for a specific Dashboard change in that conversation.
